1
00:00:12,138 --> 00:00:14,098
-[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]
-[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2
00:00:14,182 --> 00:00:17,019
-[CHOKING, STRAINING]
-[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

3
00:00:18,896 --> 00:00:21,108
[STRAINING]

4
00:00:35,332 --> 00:00:36,382
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

5
00:00:50,434 --> 00:00:51,517
Helly leave?

6
00:00:51,601 --> 00:00:52,602
Yeah.

7
00:00:58,317 --> 00:00:59,967
Maybe you should get out of here.

8
00:01:01,196 --> 00:01:03,407
I know. Just wrapping up.

9
00:01:03,907 --> 00:01:05,117
Sorry, I love the work.

10
00:01:05,993 --> 00:01:07,245
[MARK CHUCKLES]

11
00:01:14,003 --> 00:01:15,004
[BEEPS]

12
00:01:29,353 --> 00:01:30,397
Jesus.

13
00:01:31,356 --> 00:01:34,318
[STRAINING] Help!

14
00:01:36,905 --> 00:01:38,239
Help!

15
00:01:41,494 --> 00:01:43,161
Goddamn it!

16
00:01:43,245 --> 00:01:45,998
[MARK PANTING, GRUNTING]

17
00:01:46,874 --> 00:01:48,251
Oh… Oh, my God.

18
00:01:49,127 --> 00:01:51,379
[MARK, MR. GRANER STRAINING]

19
00:01:51,963 --> 00:01:53,424
[GRUNTS]

20
00:01:56,302 --> 00:01:57,470
[GRUNTS]

21
00:01:58,972 --> 00:02:00,224
Is she okay?

22
00:02:03,435 --> 00:02:04,437
MARK: Helly?

23
00:02:05,939 --> 00:02:08,523
-Mark, get in the elevator.
-Helly? Helly!

24
00:02:08,607 --> 00:02:09,859
Get in the elevator!

25
00:02:13,447 --> 00:02:14,490
[SCANNER BEEPS]

26
00:02:17,452 --> 00:02:18,703
Is she okay?

27
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:27,840
-[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]
-[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

28
00:02:28,882 --> 00:02:29,932
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

29
00:02:35,348 --> 00:02:37,641
-Judd.
-Mr. Scout, you have a good evening.

30
00:02:37,725 --> 00:02:39,061
Will do. Same to you.

31
00:02:42,148 --> 00:02:43,649
[SIGHS]

32
00:04:08,624 --> 00:04:10,084
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

33
00:04:27,396 --> 00:04:28,856
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

34
00:04:29,607 --> 00:04:32,152
-[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]
-[BREATHING SHAKILY]

35
00:04:32,735 --> 00:04:34,195
[PANTING]

36
00:04:41,872 --> 00:04:43,039
Is she alive?

37
00:04:44,666 --> 00:04:46,209
Have a seat, Mark.

38
00:04:59,726 --> 00:05:02,353
-She's in the hospital.
-[EXHALES SHARPLY]

39
00:05:02,437 --> 00:05:06,400
She has severe bruising but,
thankfully, no permanent damage.

40
00:05:06,484 --> 00:05:07,943
[BREATHING SHAKILY] Okay.

41
00:05:08,611 --> 00:05:11,739
Okay, so you… You're letting her go?
[INHALES SHAKILY]

42
00:05:11,823 --> 00:05:14,117
Helly's outie has no
intention of resigning…

43
00:05:14,201 --> 00:05:16,036
She almost died.
She doesn't wanna be here.

44
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,497
And she will be back at
her desk in a few days.

45
00:05:18,581 --> 00:05:19,832
Is that enough time?

46
00:05:22,252 --> 00:05:26,173
This happened on your watch, Mark S.

47
00:05:30,136 --> 00:05:34,642
And you can thank Kier
himself it went the way it did.

48
00:05:35,392 --> 00:05:37,269
Have a productive day.

49
00:06:09,850 --> 00:06:11,434
RICKEN: <i>What is it to fail?</i>

50
00:06:12,894 --> 00:06:16,857
<i>My failure to break into the literary
world in my 20s was devastating,</i>

51
00:06:16,941 --> 00:06:18,776
<i>yet it taught me a vital lesson.</i>

52
00:06:19,486 --> 00:06:24,408
<i>That it was not me who was
wrong, but literature itself.</i>

53
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:28,329
<i>And that to truly find
my place in that world,</i>

54
00:06:28,413 --> 00:06:31,417
<i>I would first need to break it entirely.</i>

55
00:06:32,668 --> 00:06:33,752
<i>And so I did.</i>

56
00:06:33,836 --> 00:06:36,923
<i>A society with festering
workers cannot flourish,</i>

57
00:06:37,632 --> 00:06:41,136
<i>just as a man with
rotting toes cannot skip.</i>

58
00:06:43,556 --> 00:06:48,770
<i>What separates man from machine is
that machines cannot think for themselves.</i>

59
00:06:49,771 --> 00:06:53,651
<i>Also, they are made of metal,
whereas man is made of skin.</i>

60
00:06:53,735 --> 00:06:56,613
<i>If you are a soldier, do
not fight for my freedom.</i>

61
00:06:57,614 --> 00:07:01,118
<i>Fight for the freedom of the
soldier fighting next to you.</i>

62
00:07:02,203 --> 00:07:05,457
<i>This will make the war
more inspiring for you both.</i>

63
00:07:06,875 --> 00:07:09,085
<i>A good person will follow the rules.</i>

64
00:07:09,628 --> 00:07:12,089
<i>A great person will follow himself.</i>

65
00:07:12,173 --> 00:07:16,385
<i>Bullies are nothing but Bull and Lies.</i>

66
00:07:16,887 --> 00:07:21,182
<i>At the center of "Industry" is "Dust."</i>

67
00:07:21,266 --> 00:07:26,314
<i>They cannot crucify you
if your hand is in a fist.</i>

68
00:07:27,482 --> 00:07:31,487
<i>Should you find yourself contorting
to fit a system, dear reader,</i>

69
00:07:32,863 --> 00:07:36,952
<i>stop and ask if it's truly
you that must change</i>

70
00:07:37,536 --> 00:07:38,912
<i>or the system.</i>

71
00:07:42,333 --> 00:07:43,933
MR. GRANER: Ran the diagnostics.

72
00:07:44,293 --> 00:07:45,838
MS. COBEL: And?

73
00:07:46,547 --> 00:07:50,050
Full synaptic coupling.
Petey Kilmer's memory was reintegrated.

74
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:53,420
You were right, Harmony.

75
00:07:54,973 --> 00:07:56,391
We should celebrate.

76
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:04,108
I figure you'll take a beat
before telling the Board,

77
00:08:04,192 --> 00:08:06,342
especially after what
happened with Helly R.

78
00:08:09,157 --> 00:08:11,367
Jesus. You haven't told them.

79
00:08:14,705 --> 00:08:17,374
Comb the chip data for source signatures.

80
00:08:17,916 --> 00:08:20,043
It's saved, so you can keep it.

81
00:08:22,964 --> 00:08:24,090
A gift.

82
00:08:25,341 --> 00:08:27,344
Please find out who did this.

83
00:08:27,928 --> 00:08:30,973
I'd like to deliver everything
to the Board at once.

84
00:08:31,891 --> 00:08:32,976
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

85
00:08:41,068 --> 00:08:42,693
Oh, shit.

86
00:08:42,777 --> 00:08:44,197
<i>Hi, Mark, it's Ricken.</i>

87
00:08:44,281 --> 00:08:47,659
<i>Listen, I know you're still
in, um, severed Mark form,</i>

88
00:08:47,743 --> 00:08:51,705
<i>but, uh, Devon's at 4 centimeters,
so this baby is officially coming.</i>

89
00:08:51,789 --> 00:08:54,166
<i>Uh, we're headed to
the birthing retreat now,</i>

90
00:08:54,250 --> 00:08:55,585
<i>so please come.</i>

91
00:08:55,669 --> 00:08:57,504
<i>Mark, Ricken again.</i>

92
00:08:57,588 --> 00:09:00,842
<i>We're at the retreat, and the child
is continuing toward the birth canal,</i>

93
00:09:00,926 --> 00:09:03,469
<i>so it would be really
great if you were here.</i>

94
00:09:03,553 --> 00:09:06,807
[STAMMERS] <i>I don't know if they
let you have your phone down there…</i>

95
00:09:06,891 --> 00:09:10,018
<i>Oh, actually, if this is Mark's work self,</i>

96
00:09:10,102 --> 00:09:12,647
<i>please tell him Ricken
said to come quickly.</i>

97
00:09:12,731 --> 00:09:15,984
<i>Mark, we're still here.
Wondering if you're lost.</i>

98
00:09:16,068 --> 00:09:17,694
<i>We are in cabin six,</i>

99
00:09:17,778 --> 00:09:20,197
<i>which is through the gate
and at the end of the row.</i>

100
00:09:20,281 --> 00:09:22,867
<i>It's, um, one of the more
affordably sized units,</i>

101
00:09:22,951 --> 00:09:24,578
<i>but you should be able to find it.</i>

102
00:09:24,662 --> 00:09:26,247
<i>Please do come soon.</i>

103
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,967
Oh, hey.

104
00:09:37,051 --> 00:09:38,427
Hey. [CHUCKLING] Hey.

105
00:09:40,596 --> 00:09:42,724
Did you forget that I was gonna be here?

106
00:09:45,269 --> 00:09:46,979
-Slightly. [CHUCKLES]
-Mmm.

107
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:53,195
Look, I'm, uh, sorry
about the other night. I…

108
00:09:53,904 --> 00:09:55,489
Yeah, no, it's fine.

109
00:09:56,699 --> 00:09:57,700
Yeah.

110
00:09:59,077 --> 00:10:00,953
-She's doing great, by the way.
-Yeah?

111
00:10:01,037 --> 00:10:01,871
-Yeah.
-Okay.

112
00:10:01,955 --> 00:10:05,042
The contractions are
about 20 minutes apart,

113
00:10:05,126 --> 00:10:06,586
so we still have some time.

114
00:10:07,587 --> 00:10:10,841
Ricken is doing this thing
where he cries over her.

115
00:10:11,508 --> 00:10:13,843
-So, I'm…
-[CHUCKLES]

116
00:10:13,927 --> 00:10:16,054
I'm giving them some privacy.

117
00:10:19,559 --> 00:10:20,768
Sounds good.

118
00:10:24,815 --> 00:10:27,610
Hey, thank you for, uh,
you know, taking care of her.

119
00:10:29,362 --> 00:10:30,739
Yeah. Of course.

120
00:10:39,583 --> 00:10:42,210
[CRYING] Babe, I just
don't wanna be like my father.

121
00:10:42,294 --> 00:10:45,673
I know, baby. I think it's
good you're getting it out now.

122
00:10:46,841 --> 00:10:48,134
-[SOBS]
-It's okay.

123
00:10:49,385 --> 00:10:50,935
Hey. I'm looking for baby camp?

124
00:10:51,472 --> 00:10:55,642
Ooh. [CHUCKLES] The uncle-to-be.
Welcome, Mark.

125
00:10:55,726 --> 00:10:57,603
Yay! I'm so glad you're here.

126
00:10:57,687 --> 00:11:00,148
I didn't know if they were gonna
wake you up from work or whatever.

127
00:11:00,232 --> 00:11:02,609
Oh, no, I just saw the
message when I got off. Sorry.

128
00:11:02,693 --> 00:11:04,487
No, it's been pretty boring so far.

129
00:11:05,196 --> 00:11:09,409
All right. Well, uh, glad to
be here in this cozy nook.

130
00:11:09,493 --> 00:11:11,161
-Wow.
-Dude, did you see the one next door?

131
00:11:11,245 --> 00:11:14,165
-Yeah.
-It's, like, psychotically expensive.

132
00:11:14,249 --> 00:11:16,542
It's like a freakin' lodge.
I hate whoever's in there.

133
00:11:16,626 --> 00:11:19,253
It's just fat cats making fat kittens.

134
00:11:19,337 --> 00:11:20,339
[YAWNING] Yeah.

135
00:11:21,549 --> 00:11:23,133
-[GROANS]
-Oh, shit.

136
00:11:23,217 --> 00:11:24,217
It's a contraction.

137
00:11:24,301 --> 00:11:27,263
-Fuck.
-Mark, say a secret quickly.

138
00:11:27,347 --> 00:11:28,947
DEVON: He doesn't have to, babe.

139
00:11:29,474 --> 00:11:32,227
-What?
-The fetus is drawn to clear air.

140
00:11:32,311 --> 00:11:35,647
Purging secrets can create a
soul void that speeds the labor.

141
00:11:35,731 --> 00:11:37,233
Okay, and we want that?

142
00:11:37,317 --> 00:11:39,152
-Oh, we do.
-Hey, baby, not right now.

143
00:11:39,236 --> 00:11:42,447
It's fine, I'll start. Um, Mark…

144
00:11:43,533 --> 00:11:45,659
I love you, and I feel hurt
that you haven't called me

145
00:11:45,743 --> 00:11:47,193
to thank me for the book yet.

146
00:11:47,662 --> 00:11:50,207
-[EXHALES SHARPLY] There. Good.
-The book?

147
00:11:50,291 --> 00:11:53,001
We left a copy of his new
book on your doorstep.

148
00:11:53,085 --> 00:11:55,838
Five days ago. Five full days.

149
00:11:55,922 --> 00:11:58,466
Okay, well, I definitely
haven't seen that.

150
00:11:58,550 --> 00:12:00,719
I mean, it must've been
stolen or something. I…

151
00:12:00,803 --> 00:12:02,221
-What?
-[DEVON GROANS]

152
00:12:02,305 --> 00:12:03,972
-That was an advanced copy.
-[GROANING]

153
00:12:04,056 --> 00:12:08,019
Oh, my God. Oh, my God. Oh!

154
00:12:08,103 --> 00:12:10,522
-Are you okay?
-Oh, my God. [SIGHS]

155
00:12:10,606 --> 00:12:11,606
-I'm okay.
-RICKEN: Whew!

156
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:13,234
It's fine. It's all fine.

157
00:12:15,153 --> 00:12:16,529
Ooh.

158
00:12:16,613 --> 00:12:20,492
Okay, okay. I'm okay. Are you okay?

159
00:12:20,576 --> 00:12:21,702
Okay.

160
00:12:22,286 --> 00:12:23,747
-I'm good.
-Yeah?

161
00:12:24,456 --> 00:12:26,833
-Yeah, I'm gonna go get coffee.
-Really?

162
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:29,503
Yeah. I think. I'm gonna get going.

163
00:12:29,587 --> 00:12:32,465
-Are you sure? Um…
-Thank you. Oh, thanks, bud.

164
00:12:34,050 --> 00:12:35,593
-All right. I'll be back.
-RICKEN: Yeah.

165
00:12:35,677 --> 00:12:36,970
Okay. Be careful.

166
00:12:39,848 --> 00:12:40,850
[DOOR CLOSES]

167
00:12:45,188 --> 00:12:47,524
Well, this is good.
We can finish setting up the room.

168
00:12:47,608 --> 00:12:48,943
Um… [SMACKS LIPS] Oh.

169
00:12:51,028 --> 00:12:52,112
[GRUNTS]

170
00:12:53,490 --> 00:12:55,534
Mark, would you help me hang the kelp?

171
00:12:56,952 --> 00:12:58,538
Hang the kelp? Why?

172
00:12:59,914 --> 00:13:01,714
Do you really want me to explain it?

173
00:13:04,670 --> 00:13:07,256
[DEVON SHIVERS]

174
00:13:13,304 --> 00:13:14,305
Hi.

175
00:13:17,726 --> 00:13:19,895
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

176
00:13:21,982 --> 00:13:23,191
Hi. Excuse me?

177
00:13:24,276 --> 00:13:25,277
Sir?

178
00:13:26,152 --> 00:13:27,363
Sir… [GROANS]

179
00:13:30,825 --> 00:13:31,951
Hey.

180
00:13:32,870 --> 00:13:35,581
What the fuck, man? Oh, my Go…

181
00:13:37,207 --> 00:13:39,794
Hi, I'm so sorry.
I'm another pregnant lady.

182
00:13:39,878 --> 00:13:42,755
I'm from over there.
I just came out on a coffee run,

183
00:13:42,839 --> 00:13:45,759
and I got distracted
by your beautiful coffee,

184
00:13:45,843 --> 00:13:48,943
and I was wondering if there's
any chance you could hook me up.

185
00:13:50,765 --> 00:13:52,391
Um, okay.

186
00:13:52,475 --> 00:13:55,478
Yeah? Yes. Thank you. Thank Christ.

187
00:13:57,565 --> 00:13:59,233
[DOOR OPENS]

188
00:13:59,317 --> 00:14:00,818
[STRAINS] Hi. Thank you so much.

189
00:14:00,902 --> 00:14:03,572
-[PANTS] I'm gonna squeeze right past you.
-[CHUCKLES]

190
00:14:08,328 --> 00:14:10,538
Ooh. I'm Devon.

191
00:14:11,206 --> 00:14:12,331
Gabby.

192
00:14:12,415 --> 00:14:14,251
Thank you for narcotics.

193
00:14:15,085 --> 00:14:17,671
My husband is driving me fucking crazy.

194
00:14:18,214 --> 00:14:21,759
My brother's… depressing me.

195
00:14:21,843 --> 00:14:22,844
[CHUCKLES]

196
00:14:24,471 --> 00:14:25,723
Is it your first?

197
00:14:26,474 --> 00:14:27,767
Yeah. Yours?

198
00:14:28,559 --> 00:14:29,769
My third.

199
00:14:30,686 --> 00:14:32,022
I'm naming him William.

200
00:14:32,689 --> 00:14:36,944
Three kiddos. I'm so fucking scared
of ruining one child. [CHUCKLES]

201
00:14:37,028 --> 00:14:38,571
How do you handle it?

202
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,616
-Lotta help, I guess.
-Yeah.

203
00:14:42,116 --> 00:14:45,538
Holy shit, by the way, how
about this cabin? It's so nice.

204
00:14:46,330 --> 00:14:47,373
Are you rich?

205
00:14:48,667 --> 00:14:49,876
[LAUGHS]

206
00:14:54,173 --> 00:14:58,302
RICKEN: Because really…
if the thief reads the book,

207
00:14:58,386 --> 00:14:59,736
it will have been worth it.

208
00:15:00,389 --> 00:15:03,517
In fact, I bet you he
turns himself in afterward.

209
00:15:05,770 --> 00:15:10,608
Listen, I know the last time you were
in a medical facility was for Gemma.

210
00:15:12,027 --> 00:15:14,613
Oh, is that what this is?
A medical facility?

211
00:15:16,824 --> 00:15:20,774
Of course, the baby's middle name could've
been so lovely a tribute to her, but…

212
00:15:21,705 --> 00:15:24,542
I understand you were
unable to be comfortable with it.

213
00:15:25,084 --> 00:15:28,672
Your kid deserves her
own name without some…

214
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:31,925
Big, feely baggage.

215
00:15:41,020 --> 00:15:42,313
Yes.

216
00:15:42,938 --> 00:15:44,106
[SHIVERING] Ooh.

217
00:15:45,107 --> 00:15:48,486
-[BREATHES HEAVILY]
-[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

218
00:15:52,867 --> 00:15:54,118
DEVON: Psst.

219
00:15:55,328 --> 00:15:56,495
I got coffee.

220
00:15:58,582 --> 00:16:00,250
Toll, please.

221
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:01,376
[GROANS]

222
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:05,673
I made friends with the
richest lady in baby camp.

223
00:16:05,757 --> 00:16:06,841
[CHUCKLES]

224
00:16:06,925 --> 00:16:07,967
She was…

225
00:16:08,843 --> 00:16:10,387
Quiet, but she was nice.

226
00:16:11,055 --> 00:16:13,599
Very cute. I should send you up there.

227
00:16:14,433 --> 00:16:16,477
I'd imagine she's spoken for.

228
00:16:16,561 --> 00:16:17,562
[CHUCKLES]

229
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:21,108
I bet Alexa would give you another shot.

230
00:16:23,277 --> 00:16:24,820
I bet she wouldn't.

231
00:16:25,821 --> 00:16:28,325
-I bet you could ask her.
-Oh. Okay.

232
00:16:29,284 --> 00:16:33,372
-Ah. [GROANS]
-You okay? Do you want me to go get her?

233
00:16:33,456 --> 00:16:36,000
No, no, no.
Hold on, can I squeeze your hand?

234
00:16:36,084 --> 00:16:37,793
Yeah. There we go.

235
00:16:37,877 --> 00:16:39,777
-[GROANS, BREATHES HEAVILY]
-All right.

236
00:16:43,259 --> 00:16:46,179
-Need me to tell a secret?
-[CHUCKLES] Yeah, go ahead.

237
00:16:46,263 --> 00:16:47,930
Give me your dark shit.

238
00:16:48,014 --> 00:16:50,101
Well, so, uh…

239
00:16:52,937 --> 00:16:54,146
Um…

240
00:17:00,237 --> 00:17:04,617
I kinda think Lumon
might be up to something.

241
00:17:05,243 --> 00:17:07,955
What do you mean?
Like, with your paychecks?

242
00:17:08,956 --> 00:17:13,460
No, I've just been hearing stuff.
Just around.

243
00:17:14,129 --> 00:17:15,505
