[LAUGHING]

486
00:37:17,623 --> 00:37:23,505
-I'm… I'm sorry you had to do this.
-[LAUGHS] It's all right.

487
00:37:23,589 --> 00:37:25,298
I mean, you know that

488
00:37:25,382 --> 00:37:30,764
relationships beyond the, uh,
platonic are frowned upon anyway.

489
00:37:33,976 --> 00:37:35,686
Is that what we are?

490
00:37:36,812 --> 00:37:38,105
[DYLAN CLEARS THROAT]

491
00:37:39,064 --> 00:37:43,736
Well, uh, Burt G., at this time I, uh,

492
00:37:43,820 --> 00:37:48,993
formally release you
from MDR's supervision.

493
00:37:49,494 --> 00:37:52,998
As Kier said, "Be ever merry."

494
00:37:56,001 --> 00:37:57,301
Would you like to come in?

495
00:37:58,296 --> 00:38:01,424
There is something in the
storeroom I'd like to show you.

496
00:38:04,011 --> 00:38:05,554
And Dylan, of course.

497
00:38:07,097 --> 00:38:08,558
[MOUTHING WORDS]

498
00:38:10,936 --> 00:38:14,232
IRVING: <i>The Courtship of Kier and Imogene.</i>

499
00:38:15,191 --> 00:38:19,612
He met his wife while a
stewman in an ether factory.

500
00:38:21,073 --> 00:38:22,991
Damn dumb being here.

501
00:38:23,575 --> 00:38:25,536
She was a swab girl.

502
00:38:26,037 --> 00:38:29,958
The handbook just says they
were bonded by the spirit of industry.

503
00:38:30,792 --> 00:38:34,296
BURT: I know, but if this
interpretation is correct,

504
00:38:34,380 --> 00:38:38,926
they met as colleagues.
Took heart to each other as colleagues.

505
00:38:39,010 --> 00:38:40,887
-Mmm.
-Hmm.

506
00:38:47,436 --> 00:38:52,442
Makes you wonder how
something could be wrong if Kier…

507
00:38:52,526 --> 00:38:55,404
-Get away from him! You lying fuck!
-BURT: Dylan, what?

508
00:38:55,488 --> 00:38:56,781
-Dylan!
-He claims he doesn't know

509
00:38:56,865 --> 00:38:59,283
about this painting, meanwhile,
it's sitting on his shelf.

510
00:38:59,367 --> 00:39:01,829
-That isn't.
-DYLAN: Irv, we need to go. Now.

511
00:39:02,621 --> 00:39:03,956
It's not the same.

512
00:39:04,623 --> 00:39:06,167
-What?
-Look.

513
00:39:06,251 --> 00:39:08,878
Look at the badges
the raiders are wearing.

514
00:39:08,962 --> 00:39:12,925
That's not O&D, Dylan. It's us.

515
00:39:14,177 --> 00:39:16,971
This one's never gone
into the hallway rotation.

516
00:39:17,597 --> 00:39:20,100
It's called <i>"The Macrodata
Refinement Calamity."</i>

517
00:39:20,184 --> 00:39:21,935
Okay, but we've never
done anything like that.

518
00:39:22,019 --> 00:39:25,069
Why the hell would there be
two versions of the same painting?

519
00:39:37,287 --> 00:39:40,248
HELLY: I mean, what if
the goats are the numbers?

520
00:39:40,332 --> 00:39:43,794
Like, we're deciding which goats
live and which ones… Oh, God.

521
00:39:43,878 --> 00:39:45,129
I doubt it's that.

522
00:39:45,213 --> 00:39:46,715
Look, um…

523
00:39:48,342 --> 00:39:51,178
I know you don't wanna be here. But…

524
00:39:52,764 --> 00:39:54,432
I'm glad you are.

525
00:39:56,226 --> 00:40:00,648
And I'm sorry that this is
the best I can do right now.

526
00:40:04,277 --> 00:40:06,327
If you give me the map, I'll clean it up.

527
00:40:09,992 --> 00:40:11,452
Your drawing is shit.

528
00:40:11,536 --> 00:40:12,870
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

529
00:40:16,208 --> 00:40:18,209
Oh. Hi, uh, Ms. Casey.

530
00:40:18,293 --> 00:40:21,088
We were just heading back
from our mental health walk.

531
00:40:21,923 --> 00:40:23,633
You're both unhurt?

532
00:40:24,634 --> 00:40:25,802
We… We are.

533
00:40:26,386 --> 00:40:30,766
[SIGHS] I'm glad. I was scared.

534
00:40:31,267 --> 00:40:32,393
I'm sorry.

535
00:40:34,271 --> 00:40:35,564
I forgive you.

536
00:40:38,860 --> 00:40:40,194
Okay, then.

537
00:40:57,256 --> 00:40:58,757
-[KNOCKS]
-[DOOR OPENS]

538
00:41:00,050 --> 00:41:02,261
You aware what MDR is up to right now?

539
00:41:02,345 --> 00:41:05,474
I thought that's what you were paid for.

540
00:41:06,057 --> 00:41:07,350
You're not stopping it?

541
00:41:08,269 --> 00:41:12,106
"The surest way to tame a prisoner
is to let him believe he's free."

542
00:41:12,690 --> 00:41:14,484
There's a Kier quote for everything.

543
00:41:14,568 --> 00:41:16,528
How many more departments
are you gonna let them find?

544
00:41:16,612 --> 00:41:18,655
I'll have a word with Mark.

545
00:41:18,739 --> 00:41:22,494
I would be careful.
Upstairs wouldn't look kindly on this.

546
00:41:23,578 --> 00:41:24,913
Yes, Daddy.

547
00:41:28,209 --> 00:41:31,755
You can talk to me when you
figure out who hacked Kilmer's chip.

548
00:41:41,432 --> 00:41:43,352
Excuse me, everyone.

549
00:41:45,395 --> 00:41:49,234
I wanna introduce you
all to Irving and Dylan.

550
00:41:50,026 --> 00:41:51,486
They're from MDR.

551
00:41:52,070 --> 00:41:54,072
[MACHINES WHIRRING]

552
00:41:54,156 --> 00:41:55,241
And they're friends.

